.TH ISHARE2 1 "August 2026" "ishare2 4.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ishare2 \- download and manage network device images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ishare2
.RI [ action ]
.RI [ param1 ]
.RI [ param2 ]
.RI [ \-\-overwrite ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ishare2
is a command line tool that downloads and manages network device images (QEMU,
IOL/BIN, DYNAMIPS and DOCKER) for network emulators such as EVE-NG and UNetLab.
Images are fetched from the LabHub index and verified against their expected
size and SHA1/MD5 checksums after download.
.PP
Most actions require root privileges.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B search
Search the image index for images by type or name.
.TP
.B pull
Download an image by type and id, or download all images of a type.
.TP
.B installed
List the images currently installed on the server.
.TP
.B labs
List the \fB.unl\fR labs in the default labs directory and download the images
they require.
.TP
.B mylabs
Like \fBlabs\fR, but using a custom labs directory.
.TP
.B relicense
(alias: \fBlicense\fR) Generate a new \fBiourc\fR license for IOL (bin) images.
.TP
.B upgrade
Display a menu to upgrade \fBishare2\fR or the \fBishare2\fR GUI.
.TP
.B changelog
Show the latest changes made to \fBishare2\fR.
.TP
.B fix
Fix common issues: \fBpermissions\fR, \fBdns\fR or \fBblock_cisco\fR.
.TP
.B logs
Show or clear the \fBishare2\fR log file using \fBshow\fR or \fBclear\fR.
.TP
.B gui
Install, start, stop or restart the \fBishare2\fR web interface.
.TP
.B config
Run the interactive configuration wizard.
.TP
.B test
Test connectivity to the services \fBishare2\fR depends on.
.TP
.B help
Show usage information.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed and latest \fBishare2\fR versions.
.SH IMAGE TYPES
The \fBsearch\fR, \fBpull\fR and \fBinstalled\fR actions use the following
image types:
.TP
.B qemu
QEMU virtual machine images.
.TP
.B iol
(alias: \fBbin\fR) Cisco IOS on Linux (IOL) images.
.TP
.B dynamips
Dynamips (Cisco IOS) images.
.TP
.B docker
Docker images (the \fBinstalled\fR action only).
.TP
.B all
Every type; with \fBpull\fR it downloads every image of the given type.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Replace an existing image instead of reporting that it already exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
Search for images:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ishare2 search all
ishare2 search qemu
ishare2 search bin
ishare2 search vios
ishare2 search qemu vios
.RE
.fi
.PP
Download an image:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ishare2 pull qemu 242
ishare2 pull bin 5
ishare2 pull dynamips 2
ishare2 pull dynamips all
ishare2 pull qemu 242 \-\-overwrite
.RE
.fi
.PP
List installed images:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ishare2 installed all
ishare2 installed qemu
ishare2 installed docker
.RE
.fi
.PP
Download images for a lab:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ishare2 labs
ishare2 labs 1
ishare2 labs all
ishare2 mylabs /path/to/labs
ishare2 mylabs /path/to/labs 1
ishare2 mylabs /path/to/labs all
.RE
.fi
.PP
Other actions:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ishare2 relicense
ishare2 upgrade
ishare2 changelog
ishare2 fix permissions
ishare2 logs show
ishare2 gui install
ishare2 config
ishare2 test
ishare2 help
ishare2 \-\-version
.RE
.fi
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is stored in
.B /etc/ishare2.conf
. Additional settings can be placed in drop-in files under
.B /etc/ishare2.d/
(matching \fB*.conf\fR), which are sourced after the main configuration. Run
.B ishare2 config
to configure interactively.
.TP
.B AUTO_FIX_PERMISSIONS
When \fBtrue\fR, fix image permissions automatically after a download. It
defaults to \fBfalse\fR; set it in the wizard or run
.B ishare2 fix permissions
manually.
.SH SECURITY
Some images include shell (\fB.sh\fR) or PHP (\fB.php\fR) scripts. \fBishare2\fR
warns before downloading such files and lets you skip them, and warns when one
is found inside an extracted archive. Only run or install scripts from sources
you trust.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/ishare2.conf
Main configuration file.
.TP
.B /etc/ishare2.d/
Drop-in configuration directory.
.TP
.B /var/log/ishare2.log
Log file.
.TP
.B /opt/ishare2/cli/
State directory (image index, modules).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ISHARE2_LOG_FILE
Override the log file location (default: \fB/var/log/ishare2.log\fR).
.TP
.B DEV
Set \fBDEV=true\fR when running the installer to install the \fBdev\fR branch
instead of \fBmain\fR.
